{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1200094-thrown-weapons-rule-inconsistency","id":1200094,"title":"Thrown Weapons rule inconsistency","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-03-27T09:59:38-07:00","id":1200094,"title":"Thrown Weapons rule inconsistency","content":"So on page 288 of C20, it explains the difficulty ratings for thrown weapons and explains that all thrown weapons have a range of 10 yards/meters. It then explains how ranged weapons works, but immediately follows this up with a chart explaining how all thrown weapons always have a difficulty of 6 for 0-2 yards (point blank), 6 again for up to 10 yards, and 8 for 10-20 yards. <br /> <br /> So... what the heck? How do difficulty values work with thrown weapons?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/19264-slanzer","name":"Slanzer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-29T09:37:14-07:00","id":1200839,"title":"","content":"Do the first set of difficulties contradict the second ones, and if so, how? I don't currently have my book to hand, but the difficulty values you've given don't seem contradictory (although the point-blank difficulty seems superfluous when they could've just written one difficulty for the whole 0-10m range).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-30T12:10:10-07:00","id":1201352,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1200094-thrown-weapons-rule-inconsistency?p=1200839#post1200839\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do the first set of difficulties contradict the second ones, and if so, how? I don't currently have my book to hand, but the difficulty values you've given don't seem contradictory (although the point-blank difficulty seems superfluous when they could've just written one difficulty for the whole 0-10m range).</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, very much so. The first chart lists difficulties ranging from 5-7 depending on the individual thrown weapon and the explanation says that thrown weapons have a max range of 10m. The second chart then explains that all thrown weapons have a difficulty of 6 for 0-2m, all thrown weapons have a difficulty of 6 for normal range (10m), and all thrown weapons have a difficulty of 8 for long range (double normal, so 20m).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/19264-slanzer","name":"Slanzer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-07T09:57:46-07:00","id":1204205,"title":"","content":"The second part of that sounds like the 'wrong' bit, increasing difficulty so steeply for long range results in very few people even bothering.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11490-dogstar","name":"Dogstar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11490_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}